CHAPTER V
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 30
protection of women victims The Regional Government is obligated to: of violence,
a. guarantee the implementation of the fulfillment of women's rights and the provision of assurance of safety from acts of violence, and efforts of exploitation against women in the region;
b. establish policies, programs, activities for the protection of women and guarantees for handling victims to eliminate all forms of discrimination and acts of violence against women in the region;
c. provide guidance and supervision in efforts to protect women carried out by Regional Apparatus handling the Protection and Empowerment of Women;
d. endeavor to establish institutions for the protection of women;
e. establish policies, programs and activities for the protection of women that have been determined; and
f. conduct socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of women victims of violence and discrimination;

Article 14
(1) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women as referred to in Article 13, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus with authority over matters of:
a. health;
b. education;
c. manpower;
d. socio-political affairs;
e. protection and empowerment of women; and
f. peace and order;
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan with the Regional Apparatus with authority over Protection and Empowerment of Women.
